Printing press doing job work (Printing books on paper supplied by author): Composite supply of service (printing is principal supply).

Customs bonded warehouse goods sold multiple times before clearance (High Sea Sales): Neither supply of goods nor services (Schedule III) - IGST charged only once at final port clearance.

Personal vehicle sold to Cars24: Normal individual not in business of selling cars, so sale is not supply, no GST. Cars24 sells it on margin scheme.

Rule 42 & 43 complexities for real estate developers transitioning from under-construction (taxable) to OC received (exempt) status and reversing millions in ITC.

ISD (Input Service Distributor) mechanism vs Cross Charge: When is raising a tax invoice better than distributing credit via GSTR-6?

Action against fake invoices: Section 132(1)(b) criminalizing issuing invoices without supply. Arrest threshold > 2 Crores.

Attachment of property (Section 83): Commissioner attaching factory premises during a raid to prevent promoter from selling assets and fleeing.

Search and Seizure (Section 67): Officers confiscating laptops, hard drives, and mobile phones as digital evidence during EA-2000 audits.

Pan-masala / Gutkha manufacturers mandatory machine registration to prevent unaccounted unbilled manufacturing evasion (Special procedure 2024).

Rectification of Mistake (ROM) under Section 161: Correcting an obvious typographical error in a GST appeal order within 3 months.

Stay on recovery of demand: Paying 10% pre-deposit automatically stays the recovery of the remaining 90% balance pending appeal.

Condonation of delay for filing appeals beyond 3 months: High courts invoking Article 226 strictly only if technical glitch proven, rejecting negligence.

Audit by Tax Authorities (Section 65): Department initiating comprehensive 3-5 year desk/field audit, culminating in Audit Report ADT-02 and potential DRC-01 SCN.

Special Audit (Section 66): Department forcing a taxpayer to get accounts audited by an empanelled CA/CMA if complex fraud/valuation suspected.

E-commerce operator liability under Section 9(5): Urban Company (plumbers, beauticians) and MakeMyTrip (hotels) explicitly liable to pay tax as if they are the supplier.

TCS by Swiggy/Zomato (1%) vs Section 9(5) liability (5%): Cloud kitchens (5%) vs selling a cake via Instamart (1% TCS) differentiation.

Aggregator model vs Marketplace model: Is Amazon a pure agent or an operator, determining place of supply and GST tracking.

OIDAR services compliance: Foreign entities (Zoom, Spotify) must appoint a representative in India and register in Form GST REG-10 to remit 18% IGST.

Government exempt services (Article 243W): Panchayat and municipality services like birth/death certificates, water supply non-taxable.

Toll charges on highways (NHAI/Fastag): Excluded from GST. But FASTag issuance convenience fee charged by bank attracts 18% GST.

Railway ticket cancellation charges: Retaining 100 rupees for cancellation is tolerating an act? Indian Railways charging GST on cancellation fees.

Tour operator services (Outbound tours): Indian tour operator booking Dubai package for Indian client - Place of supply is outside India? (Exemption debates).

Foreign exchange conversion services by banks (Forex dealers): Specialized GST valuation mechanism (e.g. 1% of gross amount or slab-based composition).

Air ticket booking agent margin vs gross value: IATA commission vs convenience fee GST valuation rule 32(3).

Life insurance premium GST: Term life (18% on total premium) vs Endowment (4.5% first year, 2.25% renewal) specialized valuation mimicking saving/investment split.

Annuity/Pension plan single premium GST valuation: 1.8% of the single premium charged as GST liability by LIC/private insurers.

Second-hand goods (Margin Scheme) Rule 32(5): Buying old laptop for 10,000, selling for 12,000. GST (18%) only applies to the 2,000 margin. If sold at a loss, GST is zero.

Supply of actionable claims: Lottery, betting, gambling are actionable claims heavily taxed, but other actionable claims (like unsecured debt transfer) are Schedule III non-GST.

Notice under Section 79 (Recovery of tax): Garnishee proceedings where GST officer writes to taxpayer's clients (Debtors) to pay the GST department directly instead of the taxpayer.

Inverted duty structure on railway wagons and locomotives: Supreme court upholding the denial of ITC refund on input services under the formula.

Supply of solar power plant (EPC contract): Composite supply where 70% value deemed as goods (solar panels 12%) and 30% as services (installation 18%).

Job work vs Manufacturing: Can an alcohol bottling plant claim job worker status (18%) or is it manufacturing a non-GST product?

Cross-empowerment gridlock: Can DGGI issue an SCN (Show Cause Notice) to a taxpayer assigned to the State GST jurisdiction? (Yes, authorized by CBIC).

Re-credit of reversed ITC on payment to supplier after 180 days: Re-claiming it does NOT have a time limit (Section 16(4) 30th Nov limit doesn't apply to re-claims).

Section 16(2)(aa) impact: Buyer loses ITC if supplier makes a clerical mistake transferring B2B invoice to B2C. The stringent matching causing massive working capital blocks.

Non-payment of GST by supplier: Buyer facing DRC-01A recovery notices under the "Twin conditions" rule. Taxpayer defense citing "impossible to perform / Lex non cogit ad impossibilia".

Writ of Mandamus in High Courts to unlock ITC frozen under Rule 86A beyond the 1-year statutory limit.

GST Council recommendation status: Supreme court judgment (Mohit Minerals) stating GST Council recommendations are persuasive, not strictly binding on state legislatures.

The legality of "Notice Pay Recovery" subjected to GST before CBIC Circular 178 cleared the air classifying it as non-taxable employer-employee transaction.

Liquidated damages for delay in construction contract: Clarified as non-taxable measure of compensation, not a consideration for "tolerating an act".

Valuation of free diesel supplied by principal to transporter in GTA service: FOC (Free of cost) fuel must be added to freight value for GST calculation?

Warranty replacement parts shipped free of cost to customer: Manufacturer reversing ITC vs charging GST on zero-value invoice complexities.

Sale of scrap generating minor income for a hospital (exempt entity): The sale of scrap becomes taxable, forcing the hospital to take GST registration if turnover exceeds limits.

Valuation of subsidized canteen food for factory workers: Employers charging ₹10 per meal. GST applicable on nominal value or open market value? (Taxed at nominal consideration).

Free intra-state branch transfers: No GST required since it's the same GSTIN, unlike inter-state branch transfers which need IGST cross-charge.

Supply of services between related persons: A director providing rent-free property to their own private limited company. Deemed supply (Schedule I) triggering 18% GST on Open Market Value.

RCM on security lending scheme (SLB) in stock markets: Borrower of securities paying GST on lending fees under reverse charge.

E-way bill interception and minor clerical errors: Circular 64/2018 limiting penalty to ₹1,000 for typographical errors in vehicle numbers instead of 200% tax penalty.

